---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "June 10, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Almstins">
  <style>
    .privacy-hero {
      background: var(--surface-bg);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      padding: 4rem 2rem;
    }
    .hero-inner {
      max-width: 48rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .hero-inner h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-primary);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .hero-inner p {
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .hero-inner .updated {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    .privacy-content {
      max-width: 48rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 3rem 2rem;
    }

    .section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }

    .section h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-primary);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    }
    .section h3 {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-primary);
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .section p {
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .section ul {
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-left: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .section li { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .section a { color: var(--accent); }

    .callout {
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .callout p { color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
    .callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .callout strong { color: var(--accent); }

    .footer-note {
      background: var(--surface-card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
  </style>

  <div class="privacy-hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        This policy explains what Almstins collects, how we use it, who we share it with, and the
        rights you have over your data. In plain terms: your account is yours, we don't sell your
        data, and we built the product so we never hold the keys to your funds.
      </p>
      <p class="updated"><strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="privacy-content">

    <div class="section">
      <h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        Almstins ("Almstins", "we", "us") provides a crypto portfolio tracker, bookkeeping tool, and
        free wallet- and website-safety checker at almstins.com. This Privacy Policy applies to your
        Almstins account, the data you store with us, and your use of our public tools — including the
        wallet checker, which anyone can use without an account.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a deeper, plain-language explanation of how our architecture protects you, see our
        <a href="/security-and-privacy">Security &amp; Privacy</a> page. This document is the formal policy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>2. Account privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Your Almstins account is private to you. The data in it — the wallets you add, the transactions
        you import, the cost basis we calculate, the labels and settings you create — is visible only to
        you and to the limited Almstins systems required to operate the service.
      </p>
      <h3>What we collect for your account</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account identifier</strong> — your email address, or the email/ID we receive if you sign in with Google or GitHub. That's all we need to create and secure your login. Whether you sign in with email, Google, or GitHub, we store only your email address or provided ID — never a password. For maximum privacy, you can use a dedicated email address that isn't tied to your real name.</li>
        <li><strong>Wallet addresses you add</strong> — the public blockchain addresses you choose to track. These are already public on-chain; we organize them for you.</li>
        <li><strong>Transaction and cost-basis records</strong> — imported from CSV files you upload or read from the public blockchain by address: dates, amounts, prices, and any notes you add.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings and preferences</strong> — labels, alerts, and configuration you create.</li>
        <li><strong>Limited technical logs</strong> — standard server logs (such as IP address, timestamp, and response code) kept for security and debugging.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>What we never collect or store</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your private keys, seed phrases, or recovery words — we have no mechanism to access them and no ability to move, trade, or sign for your funds.</li>
        <li>Your full payment card details — all billing is handled by Stripe (see Section 6); we never see your card number.</li>
        <li>Your real name, unless you choose to put it in a note.</li>
        <li>Your browsing behavior across the web — we use no tracking pixels and no third-party advertising analytics.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>3. We do not sell your data</h2>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information — ever.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not share your data with advertisers, data brokers, or marketers. We do not build
          advertising profiles, and we do not monetize your holdings, transactions, or identity.
          Almstins makes money from subscriptions, not from your data. Under laws such as the
          California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), we do not "sell" or "share" your personal
          information as those terms are defined.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>4. Your privacy on the platform</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy isn't just a promise here — it's built into how the product works:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Read-only, no custody.</strong> Almstins reads public blockchain data by address. It never connects to your wallet, never requests signing authority, and never holds or moves funds.</li>
        <li><strong>We don't attribute addresses to identities.</strong> Almstins does not link a wallet address to a real-world person. We don't run identity de-anonymization, and we don't build "who owns what" maps. The connection between you and your addresses lives only in your own account.</li>
        <li><strong>Tenant isolation.</strong> Your data is logically isolated to your account. Other users cannot see your wallets, transactions, or activity.</li>
        <li><strong>Encryption.</strong> Sensitive data is encrypted at rest (AES-256) and in transit (HTTPS / TLS 1.3).</li>
        <li><strong>Minimal footprint.</strong> We collect only what the service needs to function. We recommend using a dedicated email address so your identity stays separate from your holdings data even in the unlikely event of a breach.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>5. How we use your information</h2>
      <p>We use the data described above only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide the service — display your portfolio, import and categorize transactions, and calculate cost basis and gains.</li>
        <li>Authenticate you and keep your account secure.</li>
        <li>Process your subscription and send essential service communications (for example, receipts or account notices).</li>
        <li>Operate, debug, and protect the service against abuse and fraud.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use your data to train advertising models, and we do not make automated decisions
        that produce legal or similarly significant effects about you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>6. Service providers we share with</h2>
      <p>
        We share data only with a small set of service providers, strictly to operate the product, and
        never for their own marketing. None of them can access your private keys or move your funds.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> (payments) — handles all billing and card processing. We store only whether your account is paid, your tier, and renewal date. PCI-DSS Level 1.</li>
        <li><strong>CoinGecko</strong> (prices) — we request historical prices; CoinGecko does not know which assets you own, only that we asked for a price on a date.</li>
        <li><strong>Blockchain explorers</strong> (e.g., Etherscan, Snowtrace, Blockstream) — we query public on-chain data for the addresses you add.</li>
        <li><strong>Google / GitHub</strong> (optional sign-in) — only if you choose them; we receive only your email or account ID.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting (Render)</strong> — our infrastructure provider, with SSL, DDoS protection, and managed security.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information if required by law, to respond to valid legal process, or to
        protect the rights, safety, and security of Almstins and its users. We will not disclose your
        data beyond what the law requires.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>7. Wallet checker &amp; safety warnings</h2>
      <p>
        Our free wallet checker and dApp/website checker query independent, third-party security
        databases (such as the MetaMask phishing blocklist, ScamSniffer, GoPlus Security, URLScan.io,
        OpenPhish, and others). How those results work is important to understand:
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Every warning means someone reported that wallet or site as a threat.</strong>
          A red or caution result reflects that one or more third-party databases have <em>reported</em>
          the address or domain. It is an attribution of what the security community has already flagged —
          not an independent determination by Almstins that something is a scam.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The absence of a warning does not guarantee that a wallet or site is safe.</strong>
          New scams appear constantly and are not reported to any database until after victims are hit.
          A clean, green, or "none found" result means only that we found no report in the sources we
          check — it is <em>not</em> a guarantee of safety. Always do your own research, and never send
          funds or connect your wallet based solely on the absence of a warning.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        The checker is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute financial,
        investment, or legal advice. Almstins is not liable for losses arising from reliance on a result.
        When you check an address or URL, we send it to those third-party services to look it up; we do not
        require an account and do not link checker queries to your identity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>8. Intended use &amp; acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Almstins exists to help you organize your own holdings and to verify the legitimacy of a wallet
        address or website before you transact. That is its purpose.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Almstins is not a surveillance tool.</strong> You may not use Almstins or its checkers
          to track, monitor, profile, stalk, harass, deanonymize, or otherwise control, target, or
          investigate another person.
        </p>
        <p>
          The wallet checker tells you whether an address or site has been <em>reported</em> as a threat —
          it does not reveal who owns an address, and it must not be used to attempt to identify, locate,
          or surveil any individual.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        We do not link addresses to real-world identities, and we expect the same of you. Using Almstins
        to infringe on another person's privacy or safety violates this policy, and may result in
        suspension or termination of your account.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your account data for as long as your account is active. When you delete your account,
        your associated data is removed and cannot be recovered. We may retain limited records where
        required for legal, tax, or security reasons (for example, billing records Stripe is required to keep).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>10. Your rights &amp; choices</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights under laws such as the GDPR (Europe) and
        CCPA/CPRA (California), including the right to access, correct, export, or delete your data, and
        the right not to have your data sold (which we do not do).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access &amp; export</strong> — request a complete export of your data (transactions, addresses, notes, settings) in JSON format by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@almstins.com">hello@almstins.com</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — delete your account and all associated data at any time from your account settings, or by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@almstins.com">hello@almstins.com</a>. Deletion takes effect immediately.</li>
        <li><strong>Correction</strong> — edit your addresses, labels, and notes directly in the app at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of these rights.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>11. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We encrypt sensitive data at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.3), host on secure managed
        infrastructure, and follow the principle of least privilege. No system is perfectly secure, but
        because Almstins never holds your private keys, even a worst-case breach cannot be used to move
        your funds. Report any security concern to <a href="mailto:security@almstins.com">security@almstins.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>12. Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We use only the cookies necessary to keep you logged in and to operate the service. We do not
        use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or third-party behavioral analytics, and we do not sell
        any data collected through cookies.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>13. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Almstins is not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from them. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>14. International users &amp; sanctions</h2>
      <p>
        Almstins is operated from the United States; if you use it from elsewhere, your data may be
        processed in the U.S. We do not knowingly serve users in comprehensively sanctioned jurisdictions
        (e.g., Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, and the Crimea, Donetsk, and Luhansk regions).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the product evolves. When we make material changes, we will update
        the "Last updated" date above and notify affected users. Continued use of Almstins after a change
        means you accept the updated policy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>16. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about your privacy or this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@almstins.com">hello@almstins.com</a>.
        For security reports, use <a href="mailto:security@almstins.com">security@almstins.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer-note">
      <p>
        <strong>Not financial or legal advice.</strong> This policy describes our privacy practices.
        Almstins is a bookkeeping and verification tool — not a custodian, broker, money transmitter, or
        investment advisor. For guidance on your specific situation, consult a qualified professional.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
